# GewyLang Canonical Grammar: Syntax v1

This grammar is normative for `language_contract.syntax_version = 1` and
defines canonical generated and repository-maintained source. The parser
accepts additional migration input, but those forms are outside this grammar
and documented only in [the migration guide](gewylang-migration.md). Stage and
version rules live in [the language and IR contract](gewylang-contract.md).

```ebnf
pipeline_file       = spacing, { documentation | comment | function_decl | spacing },
                      template_head, newline,
                      { pipeline_step | documentation | comment | spacing } ;

function_decl       = "fn", hws, ident, "(", [ param_list ], ")", hws, "=", newline,
                      { function_binding | function_step | documentation | comment | spacing } ;

template_head       = "template", hws, value ;
pipeline_step       = "|>", hws, call, newline ;
function_step       = "|>", hws, call, newline ;
function_binding    = "let", hws, ident, hws, "=", hws, value, newline ;

call                = ordinary_call | window_call ;
ordinary_call       = ident, hws, argument_list ;
window_call         = "window", "(", window_arguments, ")" ;
window_arguments    = "duration_ms", ":", optional_hws, value,
                      optional_hws, ",", optional_hws,
                      "lateness_ms", ":", optional_hws, value ;
argument_list       = argument, { optional_hws, ",", optional_hws, argument } ;
argument            = keyword_argument | value ;
keyword_argument    = ident, ":", optional_hws, value ;

param_list          = param_decl, { optional_hws, ",", optional_hws, param_decl } ;
param_decl          = ident, [ ":", optional_hws, kind_name ],
                      [ hws, "=", hws, value ] ;
kind_name           = "atom" | "bool" | "u64" | "predicate" | "narrative"
                    | "stage" | "key_event" | "phase" ;

value               = atom | string | boolean | unsigned_integer | placeholder ;
atom                = ":", atom_path ;
atom_path           = ident, { ".", ident } ;
boolean             = "true" | "false" ;
unsigned_integer    = digit, { digit } ;
placeholder         = "$", ident ;
string              = '"', { string_character }, '"' ;

documentation       = module_doc | item_doc ;
module_doc          = "//!", ? rest of line ?, newline ;
item_doc            = "///", ? rest of line ?, newline ;
comment             = line_comment | block_comment ;
line_comment        = "#", ? rest of line ?, newline ;
block_comment       = "/*", ? characters until the next */ ?, "*/" ;

ident               = ident_start, { ident_continue } ;
ident_start         = letter | "_" ;
ident_continue      = letter | digit | "_" | "-" ;
spacing             = { hws | newline } ;
hws                 = ( " " | "\t" ), { " " | "\t" } ;
optional_hws        = { " " | "\t" } ;
newline             = "\n" ;
letter              = "A" | ... | "Z" | "a" | ... | "z" ;
digit               = "0" | ... | "9" ;
string_character    = string_plain | string_escape ;
string_plain        = ? any non-control character except `"` or `\` ? ;
string_escape       = "\\", ( '"' | "\\" | "n" | "r" | "t" ) ;
```

## Semantic Constraints

- An entry contains exactly one `template :id` head.
- A malformed or empty `template` declaration is diagnosed as an invalid head, not as unrelated syntax.
- Each source file or in-memory source input is at most 256 KiB before comment stripping.
- Each pipeline call occupies one physical line.
- String escapes are decoded during lowering; every other backslash escape is invalid.
- Raw control characters are invalid inside strings; use the declared escapes for tab and line breaks.
- Parentheses inside strings are literal; unquoted nested call parentheses are invalid.
- Inline windows contain exactly one `duration_ms` and one `lateness_ms` field and no others.
- Keyword fields are unique after rule aliases are normalized.
- Argument and parameter lists contain no empty slots or trailing commas.
- Every `/*` block comment is terminated by `*/` in the same source file.
- Unquoted `=` appears exactly once in a `let` binding and at most once in a parameter default.
- Atom paths contain one or more dot-separated identifiers with no whitespace or empty segments.
- Function parameter and local binding names are bare identifiers, never atom-prefixed names.
- Keyword field names are bare identifiers; malformed names are distinct from unknown fields.
- Every keyword argument has a non-empty value after `:`.
- Function units use `fn name(...) =` and contain no braces.
- Every line beginning with the `fn` keyword is parsed as a function declaration or rejected as an invalid signature.
- Function defaults are trailing.
- Placeholders use `$name`.
- Braced, empty, numeric-leading, and suffixed placeholders are invalid.
- Source values outside the five declared lexical families are invalid.
- Strings are opaque values and never interpolate `$name` placeholders.
- Positional call arguments precede named arguments.
- Rules use named compact fields in canonical order.
- Complex colon-delimited predicates are quoted strings or local bindings.
- `let` is local and immutable inside a function unit.
- Expression functions end at the next non-comment, non-empty line that is not
  a `let` binding or pipeline step.
- `include` resolves before lowering; include cycles are rejected.
- `use` applies pure function units; recursive use cycles are rejected.
- The valid pipeline steps and value vocabularies are closed sets defined in
  [the LLM guide](gewylang-llm-guide.md) and
  [DSL reference](dsl-reference.md).

Formatting and repository mirror rules are normative in
[the canonical style standard](gewylang-style.md).
